    <statement><p>Evaluate the line integral
<m>\int_C 6 y \, dx + 4 x \, dy</m> where <m>C</m> is the
straight line path from <m>(1,1)</m> to <m>(3, 4)</m>.</p>
<p><m>\int_C 6 y \, dx + 4 x \, dy =</m> <fillin characters="45" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6\cdot \left(\frac{4-1}{2}+1\right)\mathopen{}\left(3-1\right)+4\cdot \left(\frac{3-1}{2}+1\right)\mathopen{}\left(4-1\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>C</m>:
<me>x= 1 + 2 t, \qquad y = 1 + 3 t, \qquad 0\le t \le 1,</me>
so that  <m>dx= 2\, dt</m> and <m>dy = 3\,dt</m>.  Hence
<me>\int_C 6 y \, dx + 4 x \, dy =
\int_0^1 6(1 + 3 t)2\, dt + 4(1 + 2 t)3\, dt =
\int_0^1 24 + 60 t\, dt = 54.</me>



</solution>
